# Groups HKDFGuard's security model uses (systemd-sysusers(8) format), the
# counterparts of the Windows MSI's HkdfGuardUsers and HkdfGuardDeployers:
#
#   hkdfguard            application accounts that use a KEK (give them the
#                        TPM key directory, PIN or secret file 0440, see
#                        docs/configuration.md); nothing in the library
#                        names it.
#   hkdfguard-deployers  under the production security model, the accounts
#                        whose key files hkdfguard_open_file trusts, and who
#                        may run `hkdfguard wrap`.
#
# Installed by both the .deb and the .rpm. Never removed, on uninstall or
# purge: a group created again later can get a different gid, and every
# file still carrying the old one would then belong to no group, or to
# another one.
g hkdfguard           -
g hkdfguard-deployers -
